# Phase 3 Diagrams — High Availability DNS

## Phase 3 HA DNS Architecture

![Phase 3 HA DNS Architecture](../../diagrams/04-phase-3-ha-dns.png)

## DNS Resolution and Failover Flow

![DNS Resolution and Failover Flow](../../diagrams/dns-resolution-and-failover-flow.png)

## What This Shows

- Clients use a shared DNS virtual IP.
- Keepalived moves the VIP between Pi-hole nodes during failover.
- Each Pi-hole node uses its own local Unbound recursive resolver.
- Gravity Sync keeps Pi-hole configuration aligned between nodes.
- DNS remains available if the primary node is unavailable.

## Result

Phase 3 establishes resilient local DNS with automatic failover, recursive DNS resolution, and configuration synchronization across both Pi-hole nodes.
